# Google OAuth 2.0 Client ID
# Create one at: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Authorised JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173
# Authorised redirect URIs: http://localhost:5173
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Microsoft Azure App Registration Client ID (optional — enables OneDrive auto-save)
# Steps:
#   1. Go to portal.azure.com → Azure Active Directory → App registrations → New registration
#   2. Name: NNT Editor  |  Supported account types: Accounts in any org + personal MS accounts
#   3. Redirect URI: Single-page application (SPA) → http://localhost:5173
#   4. After creation, copy the Application (client) ID below
#   5. Go to API permissions → Add → Microsoft Graph → Delegated → add: User.Read, Files.ReadWrite
# Leave blank or remove to hide the OneDrive button entirely.
VITE_MS_CLIENT_ID=your_azure_application_client_id_here
